BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BETTER OFF READ- readings & conversations with Nico Amador\, Camer
 on Awkward-Rich\, & Stephanie Burt
DTSTART:20261113T170000
DTEND:20261113T190000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:b4753246a844e249507946e84d4b83@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Out in the Open\, Everyone's Books\, & Brooks Memorial Library
  present: BETTER OFF READ It's About Time: readings & conversations with N
 ico Amador\, Cameron Awkward-Rich\, and Stephanie Burt Join us for another
  sparkling evening of trans literature and conversation! In partnership wi
 th Everyone’s Books and Brooks Memorial Library\, Out in the Open is thr
 illed to host prize-winning poets Nico Amador\, Cameron Awkward-Rich\, and
  Stephanie Burt at a beautiful new event space in downtown Brattleboro. Th
 ere will be soup\, bread\, discussion\, books for sale\, and more. Free an
 d open to the public. This program is supported by a Brattleboro Town Arts
  Fund grant. *** NICO AMADOR is a writer and educator from San Diego\, cur
 rently based in Vermont and Provincetown. Informed by his involvement in m
 ovements for social change\, his poetry is interested in acts of radical i
 magination\, place\, and belonging. CAMERON AWKWARD-RICH is a poet\, profe
 ssor\, and the author of three poetry collections\, including AN OPTIMISM
 — "a book that un-mutes possibility [and] re-imagines time\,” winner o
 f the 2026 Massachusetts Book Award. His latest project\, TIME ALSO WILL M
 AKE IT INTERESTING\, is an edited selection of the journals of writer/pain
 ter/activist Red Jordan Arobateau\, a crucial yet undersung figure in San 
 Francisco trans queer cultures. STEPHANIE BURT is a poet\, literary critic
 \, professor\, and author of 14 books\, including WE ARE MERMAIDS—a poet
 ry collection “living in the trans present and future.” Burt's groundb
 reaking anthology SUPER GAY POEMS: LGBTQIA+ Poetry After Stonewall won the
  2025 New England Book award and has been acclaimed as "a new way of think
 ing about beauty\, passion\, and the passage of time."\n\nSources: Vermont
  Public
LOCATION:Downtown Brattleboro Alliance Garage\, 22 High St.
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/better-off
 -read-readings-amp-conversations-with-nico-amador-cameron-awkward-rich-amp
 -stephanie-burt-19-10-2026-15-06-10
END:VEVENT
