BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Asylum Seekers Project (CASP) 10th Anniversary Celebrati
 on
DTSTART:20261113T163000
DTEND:20261113T190000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:3a4c99839869f965e82b40ebfa4aae@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Community Asylum Seekers Project\, aka CASP\, is celebrati
 ng our 10th anniversary! As you (hopefully) know\, we work with asylum see
 kers who are seeking refuge and citizenship in our country\, as has been o
 ffered to them by our constitution\, our welcoming people\, and the inscri
 ption on the Statue of Liberty: “Give me your tired\, your poor\, your h
 uddled masses yearning to breathe free.” CASP has been proud to support 
 this asylum seekers\, and we’re very happy to have been doing this work 
 for the last 10 years! We'll be celebrating CASP's 10th Anniversary at the
  Retreat Farm in Brattleboro\, Friday November 13\, 4:30-7pm. We'll have f
 ood\, music\, speakers\, and time to reflect on our history and where we g
 o from here. Please join us! (this is a FREE event!) Retreat Farm\n\nSourc
 es: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/community-
 asylum-seekers-project-casp-10th-anniversary-celebration-02-11-2026-15-37-
 09
END:VEVENT
