BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jukebox Turns Ten: Burlington
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261113
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261114
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:155661ba951b442a87c4b00962c125@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:It’s our tenth season of Jukebox\, and we’re playing the h
 its\, deep cuts\, and brand new songs! This series will feature wholly uni
 que programs at our three stops\, as the repertoire is chosen in real time
  from 16 possible selections. You’ll hear music from the old guard of he
 avy hitters like Beethoven and Bach\, brilliant modern composers such as J
 essie Montgomery and Caroline Shaw\, solos\, duos\, and pieces that spans 
 the myriad of different styles and genres you’ve come to expect from our
  Jukebox quartet. With the help of the audience\, the program will be deci
 ded by chance as eight pieces are picked from our “jukebox” to perform
 . Every night will be one of a kind – it’s a game where we don’t kno
 w exactly what’s coming! Don’t miss out as we celebrate ten years of t
 his fun\, eclectic\, and intimate concert series.\n\nSources: Vermont.com
 \, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Symphony Orchestra\, Burlington\, VT
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/jukebox-tu
 rns-ten-burlington-10-08-2026-13-24-18
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn from the Lawyers: A Legal Webinar for Artists
DTSTART:20261113T113000
DTEND:20261113T130000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:30b1b58798d53cc0ff08e7dc896591@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Whether you have to suffer for your art is a question best lef
 t to philosophers. How to reduce that suffering is a question for an attor
 ney. Join the Vermont Creative Network and experts from the Vermont Small 
 Business Law Center to learn how being legally prepared for pitfalls can r
 educe problems for you and your business when obstacles appear. This webin
 ar with experts from Vermont Law and Graduate School brings together tales
  from a local artist\, mixed with expertise on how their business activiti
 es could use legal planning and protections to grow and continue creative 
 activities. Learn about protecting your work through licensing contracts\,
  handling AI scraping\, limiting liability from the public in your workspa
 ce or when interacting with your art\, as well as choosing the right entit
 y structure for your business\, hiring help\, and commercial leases. Q&A t
 hroughout is encouraged. Presenters: - Jeannette Eicks\, Professor of Law
 \, The Colleges of Law\; Small Business Law Center Founder\, VLGS\; Affili
 ated Faculty\, Stanford Law School - Sage Kochavi\, Assistant Director\, V
 ermont Small Business Law Center\; Owner\, Sage Kochavi Design Accessibili
 ty: This event will be live captioned by White Coat Captioning. We strive 
 to host inclusive\, accessible events that enable all individuals to parti
 cipate. We invite you contact us with the specific accommodations you may 
 need to facilitate your participation in this workshop. We will make every
  effort to honor your requests when they are made by Oct. 30\, 2026. Reque
 sts and questions should be addressed to Michele Bailey\, Accessibility Co
 ordinator\, at mbailey@vermontartscouncil.org or 802.402.4614. Voice and r
 elay calls welcome. Online\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/learn-from
 -the-lawyers-a-legal-webinar-for-artists-08-10-2026-15-26-59
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maryna Krut\, Bandura
DTSTART:20261113T193000
DTEND:20261113T204500
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:46196ef5e2707b386c84df8aced7d3@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The Russian invasion of Ukraine transformed Bandura virtuoso M
 aryna Krut from being a singer and performer updating a beautiful traditio
 n of music to being a witness testifying around the world about the devast
 ating war in her homeland. From her temporary home in the west of Ukraine
 \, she travels to the front lines of the war to perform for soldiers. In U
 kraine\, Krut gained a national following after appearances on that countr
 y’s versions of “The X Factor” and “The Voice\,” as well as plac
 ing in Eurovision. She now also travels abroad with her bandura—a Ukrain
 ian string instrument that looks like a cross between a lute and a zither
 —relating what she has seen\, and thanking audiences for their support o
 f the Ukrainian people. Audience members are invited to stay after the per
 formance to meet Ms. Krut and talk with Middlebury College’s Ukrainian s
 tudents. They will offer cookies as a token of thanks for any voluntary do
 nations to relief charities. Artist Group Info College Box Office boxoffic
 e@middlebury.edu https://www.middlebury.edu/events/event/maryna-krut-bandu
 ra 72 Porter Field Road Middlebury \, Vermont 05753 8024436433 boxoffice@m
