BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mental Health First Aid training at UCS
DTSTART:20261113T090000
DTEND:20261113T160000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:7ff3e469f6dc6bf22433e3c4db27e7@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the more than 2.6 million First Aiders who have chosen to
  be the difference in their community. Learn how to support your friends\,
  family\, and neighbors. Adult Mental Health First Aid (MHFA) teaches you 
 how to identify\, understand\, and respond to signs of mental health and s
 ubstance use challenges among adults. You’ll build skills and confidence
  you need to reach out and provide initial support to those who are strugg
 ling. You’ll also learn how to help connect them to appropriate support.
  This training is open to the public and is currently offered at no cost\,
  however\, space is limited. For more information or to register\, contact
  MLindsey@ucsvt.org.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:United Counseling Service\, 100 Ledge Hill Drive
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/mental-hea
 lth-first-aid-training-at-ucs-19-06-2026-19-09-37
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opera Vermont Presents William Grant Still’s Costaso
DTSTART:20261113T190000
DTEND:20261113T200000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:ad552f29a2817e2e857244445fcb4c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Experience the world premiere of Costaso\, by composer William
  Grant Still and librettist Verna Arvey\, presented by Opera Vermont at Ch
 andler Music Hall. Set in the Spanish-ruled American Southwest\, this swee
 ping three-act opera follows Lieutenant Ramon Costaso and his wife as thei
 r devotion is tested by jealousy\, betrayal\, and the corruption of power.
  Their story unfolds through soaring arias\, vibrant choruses\, and a movi
 ng Act II duet between Costaso and his loyal friend Manuel. The second pro
 duction in Opera Vermont’s annual opera cycle at Chandler\, Costaso brin
 gs love\, loyalty\, and tragic sacrifice to the stage while celebrating th
 e distinctive musical voice of a trailblazing American composer. Tickets a
 re 25–65\, with $10 student tickets and free admission for children ages
  12 and under. Reserve seats: https://tickets.chandler-arts.org/events/cha
 ndlercenterforthearts/2362894\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Chandler Center for the Arts\, 71 N. Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/opera-verm
 ont-presents-william-grant-stills-costaso-27-10-2026-22-32-45
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Orgel Performs Bach and Debussy
DTSTART:20261113T193000
DTEND:20261113T210000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:c7e1e6d775059e43af2b1d6e7a3b0c@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Major critics praise concert pianist Orgel for his “subtlety
  and attention to nuance\,” “rare pathos\,” “brilliant technique\,
  sense of humor and fantasy\,” and “warmth and beauty of sound.” The
  program features Claude Debussy’s complete impressionist masterpiece Pr
 eludes\, Book 1\, and six Preludes and Fugues from J. S. Bach’s Well-Tem
 pered Klavier\, Book 2\, in an evening of dazzling contrasts and compositi
 onal prowess. A preview video playlist of the Debussy with program notes c
 an be found on the Cathedral Arts website (www.cathedralarts.org). Tickets
  can be purchased here through Seven Days.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Cathedral Church of St. Paul\, 2 Cherry Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/paul-orgel
 -performs-bach-and-debussy-02-11-2026-19-15-34
END:VEVENT
