BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vermont Theatre Company presents: An Evening of One Acts
DTSTART:20261115T190000
DTEND:20261116T160000
DTSTAMP:20261113T183559Z
UID:91ab43c0e7ca57a7d614c1a0273809@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Vermont Theatre Company announces An Evening of One Acts at th
 e Evening Star Grange in East Dummerston\, VT\, November 13 through 15. Sh
 ows are at 7 pm on Friday and Saturday and 2 pm on Sunday. VTC's Fall prog
 ram of One Act plays is a learning opportunity for new and seasoned direct
 ors to try new things and stretch themselves with contemporary material. T
 he One Acts are supported by Ben Stockman\, professional theatre director 
 and artistic director of New England Youth Theatre. The producer is VTC's 
 artistic director Jess Iris\, and Midnight's own Evangeline Rera will be s
 tage manager. This Fall's play offerings are as follows: "A Scientific Exp
 erience Unlike Any Other" by Lucy Johnston\, directed by Lucy Johnston "A 
 Scientific Experience Unlike Any Other" begins in an educational narrative
  controlled by the company DEM-EATER. Ken the CEO and Wanda the Wandera sh
 rink themselves (and the audience) into the soil\, underneath the theater
 \, where they meet locals Ant and Worm. Soon a revolutionary process of so
 cial transformation begins when the worker and the farmer take back contro
 l of their means of production. The play is funny and fantastical\, while 
 remaining grounded in our present moment. Amidst the 250th anniversary of 
 the United States\, this play envisions a united block of Earthlings again
 st extractive capitalists and asks\, where do we go from here? "Court of I
 nquiry" adapted from Agatha Christie by Miles Ledoux\, directed by Miles L
 edoux "Court of Inquiry" brings us to a (possibly haunted) country house i
 n 1920s England. It's the tail-end of a New Year's Eve party\, and when a 
 mysterious stranger arrives at the stroke of midnight\, the occupants find
  themselves delving into the house's past\, pursuing the knowledge of what
  caused the former owner to take his own life. The play is based on an ear
 ly Agatha Christie story in which two of her classic characters\, Mr. Quin
  and Mr. Satterthwaite\, meet for the first time. "Riddled With You" by Al
 ex Lockie\, directed by Laura Lockie "Riddled with You" is an intergenerat
 ional family drama that examines that which binds and tears us apart. Here
 dity\, a blessing or a curse? Is the Internet a tool for connection or div
 ision? How do family dynamics shape our choices\, whether we know it or no
 t? Written by local journalist\, Alex Lockie\, it is set here and now\, an
 d you may see yourself or someone you know in it. "Platypusary" by Andrew 
 Gerber\, directed by Lucy Webb A new play by Andrew Gerber tells the true 
 story of the platypuses in the Bronx Zoo in the 1940s and 50s — with par
 allels to The Odyssey and modern-day academia. Tickets will be available o
 n a sliding scale of $10 to $20\, both at the door or online at vermontthe
 atrecompany.org. Follow Vermont Theatre Company on Facebook and Instagram 
 for updates on this production's creative process and future calls for vol
 unteers. Founded in 1984\, the Vermont Theatre Company is an all-volunteer
 \, nonprofit organization dedicated to bringing accessible and thought-pro
 voking theatre to the greater Brattleboro community. With a commitment to 
 open auditions and inclusive participation\, VTC produces a diverse range 
 of performances each year—from Shakespeare in the Park to contemporary w
 orks and new play festivals—fostering creativity\, connection\, and comm
 unity through the performing arts. Learn more at www.vermonttheatrecompany
 .org\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Evening Star Grange\, 1008 East West Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/vermont-th
 eatre-company-presents-an-evening-of-one-acts-31-10-2026-11-31-20
END:VEVENT
